{% extends "base.j2" %}

{% block content %}
    <hgroup>
        <div>
            <h1>{{ PROGRAMME_NAME }}</h1>
        </div>
        <p>An independent catalogue of every track chosen on BBC Radio 4's {{ PROGRAMME_NAME }}</p>
    </hgroup>

    <p><a href="{{ bbc_programme_url(PROGRAMME_ID) }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">{{ PROGRAMME_NAME }}</a> is a BBC Radio 4 show in which the presenters and their guests choose and discuss several tracks, building a playlist in each episode. Each track picked is linked to the one before it, and the chain usually runs the length of a series, carrying over between episodes, and starting afresh for a new series or a one-off special.</p>

    <p>BBC Sounds lists each individual episode's tracks, but not each season or the series as a whole. This site compiles <em>all</em> of them into <a href="/{{ TRACKS_PATH }}/">one big list</a>, complete with the connection between each one, who chose it, and a link to Spotify or YouTube where available.</p>

    <dl class="facts">
        <dt>Series</dt>
        <dd>{{ all_series | length }}</dd>

        <dt>Episodes</dt>
        <dd>{{ all_series.episode_count }}</dd>

        <dt>Tracks</dt>
        <dd>{{ all_series.track_count }}</dd>

        <dt>Covering</dt>
        <dd>
            {{ all_series.first_broadcast | date_format }} to {{ all_series.last_broadcast | date_format }}
        </dd>

        <dt>Playlist</dt>
        <dd>
            <a href="{{ all_series_playlist | spotify_playlist_url }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
                The complete playlist on Spotify
            </a>
        </dd>
    </dl>

    <h2>Browse</h2>

    <ul>
        <li><a href="/{{ TRACKS_PATH }}/">Every track from every episode</a> - the complete list, by series and episode</li>
        <li><a href="/{{ ARTISTS_PATH }}/">Most-chosen artists</a> - the top {{ artist_leaderboard_amt }}, as a table and charts</li>
        <li><a href="/{{ PRESENTERS_PATH }}/">Presenters and guests</a> - who picked the most tracks</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Series</h2>

    <ul class="series-index">
        {% for series in all_series %}
            <li>
                <a href="/{{ series_path(series.number) }}/">Series {{ series.number }}</a>
                -
                <small>
                    {{ series | length }} episodes,
                    {{ series.track_count }} tracks,
                    {{ series.first_broadcast | date_format }}
                </small>
            </li>
        {% endfor %}
    </ul>

    <h2>About this project</h2>

    <p>Most of the data was gathered automatically by scraping each episode's BBC Sounds page, parsing the HTML, then querying Spotify's Web API to find a recording. Because of how that search behaves, there may be slight inconsistencies between the Spotify link and the version played on the show - e.g. a remix appearing ahead of the original. Care has been taken to identify the exact recordings where possible, using music identification software such as Shazam and SoundHound.</p>

    <p>The descriptions of how tracks relate to each other were written manually up to series 4, episode 7. After that, AI was used to speed up the process: <a href="https://github.com/openai/whisper" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Whisper</a> to transcribe each episode, then <a href="https://claude.ai/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Claude</a> and <a href="https://chat.deepseek.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">DeepSeek</a> to analyse the transcripts. The output was reviewed and corrected before being added.</p>

    <p>Although care has been taken, there will probably be a few mistakes; corrections are therefore very much welcomed!</p>

    <p>Source: <a href="https://github.com/add-to-playlist/add-to-playlist.github.io">github.com/add-to-playlist/add-to-playlist.github.io</a></p>

    <p>
        <small>
            <em>
                <strong>Disclaimer:</strong> this project is an independent compilation and
                analysis of {{ PROGRAMME_NAME }} episodes. It is not affiliated with or
                endorsed by the BBC.
            </em>
        </small>
    </p>
{% endblock %}
